      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seemed the best of available solutions to me.\n\nZephyr\u0027s cache documentation, [doc/hardware/cache/guide.rst](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/6275de3e4eac3620d31ba118eafadf6098ee4c24/doc/hardware/cache/guide.rst?plain\u003d1#L4), provides two mechanisms to disable caching applicable to our use case:\n* Disabling Caching for a Memory Region ([link](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/6275de3e4eac3620d31ba118eafadf6098ee4c24/doc/hardware/cache/guide.rst#disabling-caching-for-a-memory-region)),\n* Automatically Disabling Caching by Variable ([link](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/blob/6275de3e4eac3620d31ba118eafadf6098ee4c24/doc/hardware/cache/guide.rst#automatically-disabling-caching-by-variable)).\n\nDisabling caching for the _entire_ region, which requires annotations in devicetree, is unnecessary; it\u0027s enough to selectively disable cache for the fingerprint buffer. That\u0027s how I understand intended `FP_FRAME_SECTION` usage, designed as a variable attribute.\n\nFollowing the Zephyr documentation linked above, to disable caching for a variable, the requirements are:\n* enabled CONFIG_DCACHE (enabled in dartmonkey prj.conf),\n* enabled CONFIG_NOCACHE_MEMORY (enabled in dartmonkey prj.conf),\n* the __nocache attribute appended at the end of any uncached buffer definition.\n\nThe last requirement is satisfied by the code added in this CL.\n\nGiven that disabling caching for the entire memory region requires devicetree annotations _and_ variable attribute _and_ specific Kconfig options enabled, could you please explain why you think that approach is better?",
